{"parentUuid":"c6246582-2591-44ec-9c58-2359938d43ba","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"e89011e8-eb1e-4bfc-8125-a45c3d943a16","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"validated-dancing-bee","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01B7DFPCVdR3vzhRn7psMtUL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tasks are complete. Here's a summary of what was built:\n\n## Deliverables\n\n### Skill Documents (`/root/environment/skills/`)\n1. **rdkit-morgan-fingerprints.md** — Morgan fingerprint computation and Tanimoto similarity with RDKit\n2. **pubchempy-name-to-smiles.md** — Chemical name to SMILES conversion via PubChem API\n3. **pdf-text-extraction-pymupdf.md** — Text extraction from PDFs using PyMuPDF\n4. **tanimoto-similarity-ranking.md** — End-to-end pattern for top-K similarity ranking\n5. **cirpy-chemical-name-resolver.md** — Fallback name resolution via NIH CIR\n\n### Solution (`/root/workspace/solution.py`)\nThe function `topk_tanimoto_similarity_molecules(target_molecule_name, molecule_pool_filepath, top_k)` works as follows:\n\n1. **Resolves** the target chemical name to SMILES via PubChem (no hardcoded mapping)\n2. **Extracts** molecule names from the PDF using PyMuPDF\n3. **Resolves** each pool molecule name to SMILES via PubChem\n4. **Computes** Morgan fingerprints (radius=2, chirality=True) for all molecules\n5. **Calculates** Tanimoto similarity between target and each pool molecule\n6. **Sorts** by descending similarity, with alphabetical tie-breaking\n7. **Returns** a list of the top-k molecule names (strings)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":312,"cache_read_input_tokens":48912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":312,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXt998J19ii5osSKppN6b","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7a96a40-ed7d-4b44-b516-949dd0a18370","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:16:5